# Pinned `spec` revision the conformance runner validates against.
#
# The runner refuses to run if the spec checkout it is given is not at this
# commit (override with --allow-spec-drift when deliberately testing against
# unreleased vocabulary). Without a pin the suite silently tracks whatever is
# on spec `main`, so a run that passed yesterday can pass today for a
# different reason.
#
# To re-pin: check out the new spec revision, put its full SHA and its
# VOCAB_VERSIONS line below, run `make -C . conformance` (or
# `scripts/run_conformance.py`), and record the resulting counts in the PR.

# PINNED at d819bc2, the MERGE commit of the-cascade-protocol/spec PR #56 on
# `main` (core v3.9 / core.shapes.ttl v1.8; health v2.9, clinical v1.19,
# coverage v1.6 unchanged). Tag `vocab/core-v3.9` points at this commit (pushed
# 2026-09-08). It replaces the DRAFT pin this conformance PR opened with,
# 7aadfb6, the first commit on feat/core-3.9-patient-name; the branch carried a
# second commit (32ae425, the merged cascade.jsonld context) before merging, and
# neither touches a `*.shapes.ttl`, so the counts below were re-measured at the
# merge commit rather than carried over, and came back unchanged: 150 / 27 / 0 /
# 177, 64,043 constraint checks. The branch was cut from `main` at a5a194a, the
# pin this one replaces, and merged straight back to `main`: not stacked.
#
# WHAT MOVING THE PIN DOES: four fixtures are added and four verdicts change,
# all of them the new ones. Full suite 146 passed / 27 failed / 0 skipped / 173
# total at the previous pin, 150 / 27 / 0 / 177 here. NOT ONE PRE-EXISTING
# FIXTURE CHANGES VERDICT OR REASON — compared entry by entry across both runs,
# 0 of 173 differ — which is the release's "strictly widening" claim measured
# rather than quoted.
#
# THE FOUR NEW FIXTURES REPORT `UNSHAPED` AT THE PREVIOUS PIN, WITH ZERO
# CONSTRAINT CHECKS, and that is a stronger RED than the `NO_WARNING` the two
# `.WARN.` ones would give if they were merely unconstrained. An extended
# profile carries no `rdf:type` of its own, so at core v3.8 there is no shape in
# the entire published set that reaches an untyped `<#me>` at all: nothing could
# have noticed the empty family name or the second given name, because nothing
# was looking at the node. A `--select 'core/extended-profile*'` run at that pin
# does not even complete — the runner's own self-check aborts with "zero
# constraint checks evaluated across the entire suite", which is the same fact
# stated by the harness rather than by a verdict. All four pass here at 9
# constraint checks each.
#
# ONE MEASUREMENT WORTH RECORDING SEPARATELY, because it is evidence about the
# corpus rather than about the new fixtures. `cascade:ExtendedProfileShape`
# targets the SUBJECTS OF `cascade:dateOfBirth`, and `cascade:PatientProfile`
# nodes carry that property too, so the shape reaches eight pre-existing
# fixtures as well: profile-001, -002, -003 and -005 go 32 → 41, 76 → 85, 32 →
# 41 and 32 → 41 constraint checks, and the four genomics/phenopackets oracles
# go 53 → 62, 164 → 191, 193 → 220 and 100 → 109. Every one of the eight keeps
# its verdict and its reason exactly — the four profile fixtures still pass, the
# four phenopacket oracles still fail for the same `genomics:` reasons they
# failed for before. That is the release's claim that a `cascade:PatientProfile`
# node is also reached and passes unchanged, exercised eight times rather than
# asserted once. (profile-004 carries no `cascade:dateOfBirth` and stays at 32.)
#
# PREVIOUSLY PINNED at a5a194a, the MERGE commit of the-cascade-protocol/spec
# PR #54 on `main`. The block below is that pin's own note, kept verbatim.
# (core v3.8 / health v2.9 / clinical v1.19 / coverage v1.6; health.shapes.ttl
# v1.7, and clinical.shapes.ttl, which carries no version header of its own).
# It replaces the DRAFT pin this conformance PR
# opened with, 6b34e94, the head of the spec branch
# feat/clinical-1.19-medication-dates. That branch has since merged, by two
# steps: PR #49 merged it into feat/health-2.9-coded-allergy as 9081780, and
# PR #54 merged that into `main` as this commit. The two trees are
# byte-identical -- `git diff 6b34e94 a5a194a` is empty -- so the counts below
# were re-measured rather than carried over, and came back unchanged.
#
# 6b34e94 is in fact still reachable from `main`, as the merge preserved it, so
# unlike the draft pin before it this one was never unresolvable. That is not
# why it moves. A branch head is not a release identity: it names one side of a
# merge rather than the state `main` actually publishes, nothing guarantees it
# survives a rebase or a branch deletion, and it is not what the version tag
# points at. The pin names the commit the release is published as.
#
# Tag `vocab/clinical-v1.19` points at this commit (pushed 2026-09-07). Tags
# `vocab/health-v2.9` and `vocab/clinical-v1.18` remain on the previous pin,
# 0bdfe09, because this release ships no health: term and supersedes clinical
# v1.18. The pin resolves a SHA and depends on no tag.
#
# Previously pinned on `main` at 0bdfe09, the MERGE commit of
# the-cascade-protocol/spec PR #48 (core v3.8 / health v2.9 / clinical v1.18 /
# coverage v1.6; tags `vocab/health-v2.9` and `vocab/clinical-v1.18` point at
# that commit). 0bdfe09 is the first parent of this commit.
#
# WHAT MOVING THE PIN DID, measured with this branch's fixture set against both
# revisions: 142 passed / 31 failed / 0 skipped / 173 total and 63,771
# constraint checks at 0bdfe09, becoming 146 / 27 / 0 / 173 and 63,899 here.
# (The 0bdfe09 figure is a `--allow-spec-drift` run against a checkout of that
# commit, which is what the flag is for. It is not ratcheted and is not the
# suite's result; the suite's result is the second pair.)
#
# Exactly four verdicts changed and all four are fixtures this PR adds:
# clinical/medication-dates-health-spelling.WARN,
# clinical/medication-dates-string.WARN, health/condition-health-spelling.WARN
# and health/condition-category-diagnosis.WARN each report NO_WARNING at
# 0bdfe09 -- they are shaped, and nothing notices them, because none of the six
# new constraints exists there -- and pass here, at 61 / 59 / 28 / 26 checks
# against 55 / 55 / 21 / 21. The two .VALID fixtures this PR adds,
# clinical/medication-dates-lisinopril.VALID and
# health/condition-abatement-category.VALID, pass at BOTH revisions; the release
# is strictly widening, so passing is not what proves them. What proves them is
# the constraint check count, 55 -> 59 and 21 -> 26, which is the new property
# shapes actually evaluating. No pre-existing fixture changes verdict or reason
# -- compared entry by entry across both runs, 0 of the 167 that predate this PR
# differ, and the only four that do are the four it adds -- which is the
# release's "additive and strictly widening" claim measured rather than quoted.
#
# ONE MEASUREMENT WORTH RECORDING SEPARATELY, because it is evidence about the
# corpus rather than about the new fixtures. Seven pre-existing JSON fixtures
# (med-001 through med-007) already carried health:startDate, and med-007 also
# health:endDate. At this pin each of them reports one new sh:Warning (med-007
# two) from clinical:MedicationDateSpellingShape, and every one still PASSES,
# because a positive fixture is defined by the absence of sh:Violation. So the
# defect clinical v1.19 describes was already sitting in this repository's own
# corpus, unnoticed by anything, and the release is the first thing to see it.
#
# The +128 constraint checks are fully accounted for: +22 across the four
# fixtures whose verdict changed, and +106 across 21 that kept their verdict.
# On the medication side, +66: med-001 through med-007 at +6 each (the two
# clinical:MedicationShape date properties plus the spelling shape, which fires
# on them), med-008 through med-011, core/ai-extracted-medication.ttl and
# clinical/medication-dates-lisinopril.VALID at +4 each. On the condition side,
# +40: cond-001 through cond-007 and health/condition-abatement-category.VALID
# at +5 each, from clinical:abatementDate, clinical:category and
# health:ConditionSpellingShape on health:ConditionRecordShape.
#
# WHAT MOVING TO 0bdfe09 DID, one pin earlier: 137 passed / 30 failed / 0
# skipped / 167 total and 63,447 constraint checks at 9b13ae4, becoming
# 140 / 27 / 0 / 167 and 63,543 at 0bdfe09. Exactly three verdicts changed and
# all three are fixtures the previous conformance PR added:
# health/coded-allergy-allergen-code-string.WARN, -criticality-moderate.WARN and
# -type-sensitivity.WARN each report NO_WARNING at 9b13ae4 -- nothing notices
# them, because none of the four constraints exists there -- and pass at
# 0bdfe09. The fourth fixture, health/coded-allergy-penicillin.VALID, passes at
# BOTH revisions. All twelve fixtures that instantiate health:AllergyRecord go
# 28 -> 36 checks -- the six allergy-00*.json,
# health/status-allergy-inactive.VALID,
# health/status-allergy-entered-in-error.WARN and the four added ones -- which
# is the four new property shapes on health:AllergyRecordShape actually
# evaluating, and which accounts for the whole +96. 9b13ae4 is the MERGE commit
# of the-cascade-protocol/spec PR #32 (core v3.8 / health v2.8 / clinical v1.17
# / coverage v1.6; tags `vocab/core-v3.8`, `vocab/clinical-v1.17`,
# `vocab/coverage-v1.6` point at it; `vocab/health-v2.8` remains on the pin
# before it).
#
# WHAT MOVING TO 9b13ae4 DID, two pins earlier: exactly one verdict changed, and
# it is the one that pin's baseline predicted. clinical/status-laboratoryreport-
# in-progress.WARN.ttl -- baselined before it as a spec-owned defect (sh:node
# escalating nested sh:Warning to sh:Violation on the six document subtypes) --
# started passing: clinical v1.17 moved the two Warning bindings onto
# target-class shapes (DocumentStatusShape, DocumentReferenceStatusShape), so
# the warning fires named and nothing else does. Its KNOWN_FAILURES entry was
# removed in the same commit, per the ratchet. core v3.8 defines
# cascade:PatientReported, the provenance individual seventeen shapes already
